+# satelle substrate review gives any repo an in-depth review of its substrate
+# against the constitution, its codebase and its story history
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+1. `satelle substrate review` writes a report listing every substrate item
+   with its origin, a disposition and the evidence for it, any item the judge
+   omits shown as "not judged"; proven by a CLI test over a fixture repo with
+   a stubbed judge.
+2. Each disposition's evidence cites the repo's story history (rejections and
+   reasons, amendments, parks, rework, flaky reruns, dissent), proven by a
+   fixture-ledger test.
+3. The report lists every constitution rule with a file:line finding, "no
+   finding" or "not judged", proven by a stubbed-judge fixture test.
+
+## Design (decided)
+
+- **Judgement:** a new embedded skill `satelle-substrate-review`. It receives
+  the inventory (every principle, skill, workflow step and gate and agent
+  role, each with its full text), the evidence (every gate rejection with its
+  notes, amendment, park, rework round and dissent note from the ledger), the
+  enumerated constitution rules with their bodies and `satelle-story-shape`,
+  all in its payload, and returns JSON: one disposition per item plus the
+  constitution findings. It is dispatched through a seam `newSubstrateJudge`
+  using the repo's plan-review reviewer binding.
+- **Cost guard:** one judgement dispatch per run. Evidence is computed in Go
+  and serialised into the dispatch.
